From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OAN Messaging <messaging@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:25:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sms): send password-reset codes through the OAN
 Messaging Service

When oan_messaging_connector is installed and configured on the site, a phone-only
reset enqueues one job after commit that sends the code at once (purpose otp, a UUID4
key fixed at issue, expiring with the code and at most 30 minutes). The code lives only
in the job arguments; logs and the Error Log carry reset_request_id, the OAN id and
error codes. Without the connector, Frappe's own SMS sender is used exactly as before.
The requester's response is unchanged in every case, and no failure of the job can carry the code or phone into a log.
